<Configuration>
  <!--
    Windows Sandbox harness for the POST-RELEASE END-TO-END FEEDBACK SMOKE TEST.

    Sibling of installer-test.wsb, and deliberately a different thing. That one proves the
    installer stands alone on a clean machine. THIS one proves the whole feedback pipeline
    works from a machine that has only ever seen the PUBLISHED artifact: download the release
    installer, verify it against the published SHA256SUMS.txt, install it silently, plant a
    mocked EverQuest log, launch the installed app with EQ_SMOKE_FEEDBACK set, and let it file
    ONE real bug report with a log slice attached through the ordinary submit path.

    DIFFERENCES FROM installer-test.wsb, both load-bearing:
      * NO release/ MAPPING. The installer is DOWNLOADED from
        https://github.com/jmoyers/everquest-companion/releases/latest/download/ - testing the
        artifact a user would actually get, not a local build. Networking is therefore
        required (it is on by default; do not add <Networking>Disable</Networking>).
      * The results folder is a TWO-WAY channel: the host writes the run's nonce and the
        synthesized log into it before launch, and the guest writes its verdict back.

    ON-DEMAND ONLY. This files a REAL report against the LIVE ingest API and costs a real row
    and a real S3 object (which the host then deletes). It is not in CI, not in `npm test`,
    and not in `npm run test:e2e`.

    DO NOT launch this file directly. Run it through the wrapper:
      npm run smoke:release
      (powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\sandbox\run-smoke-feedback.ps1)
    which generates the nonce, synthesizes the log, closes stale VMs (only ONE sandbox
    instance is allowed machine-wide), parks the VM window off the primary monitor without
    stealing focus, force-closes it when the results land, THEN verifies the report and its
    scrubbed slice in the live cloud and deletes both. Raw double-click skips all of that,
    leaves a VM on screen, and leaves a report in the operator's backlog.

    Read: scripts\sandbox\results\smoke-result.txt after it finishes.

    NOTE: HostFolder paths must be ABSOLUTE. They're written for this repo's location
    (C:\Users\jmoye\everquest-companion); adjust if the repo moves.
  -->
  <MappedFolders>
    <MappedFolder>
      <HostFolder>C:\Users\jmoye\everquest-companion\scripts\sandbox</HostFolder>
      <SandboxFolder>C:\harness</SandboxFolder>
      <ReadOnly>true</ReadOnly>
    </MappedFolder>
    <MappedFolder>
      <HostFolder>C:\Users\jmoye\everquest-companion\scripts\sandbox\results</HostFolder>
      <SandboxFolder>C:\results</SandboxFolder>
      <ReadOnly>false</ReadOnly>
    </MappedFolder>
  </MappedFolders>
  <LogonCommand>
    <Command>powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -NoProfile -File C:\harness\smoke-feedback.ps1</Command>
  </LogonCommand>
</Configuration>
